## Domestic, family or sexual violence

{{resources:respect}}

**Device safety:** calls, messages and browsing may leave traces. This site does not have a quick-exit feature and cannot clear browser history or records on a phone bill. Use a safer device if possible and follow the service’s own safety guidance.

## Language and relay access

See [accessible and language support](/accessible-help).{{state-block:tis}}

## Emergency calls without a standard voice call

{{resources:relay}}

**Do not text 106 from an ordinary mobile phone.** The 106 number is for TTY/TDD. The official AccessHub page explains current NRS Chat, SMS Relay, NRS Captions, Voice Relay and TTY pathways, including registration and service limitations. Check and practise the appropriate pathway before an emergency.

Video Relay is not recommended for emergencies: operating hours are limited and emergency calls cannot be identified and prioritised in the same way. Some internet/mobile relay pathways may not identify your location; be ready to supply it.

## Tailor your preparation

{{resources:accessibility}}

Include transport, communication, medicines, carers, assistance animals and backup power for essential equipment in your own plan. {{state-block:specialist}}

